# StudentRentalsScraper – Cursor rule

This project is a **Java 21 / Maven** pipeline: **scrape → post-process → clean → geocode → APIs**. Entry point: `src/main/java/main/Orchestrator.java`.

Run via `.\srs.ps1 <command>` / `./srs.sh <command>`, or `mvn exec:java -Dexec.args="..."`. Commands: `full`, `scrape-clean`, `clean`, `geocode`, `apis`, `resume`, `status`, `help`. No arguments opens an interactive menu. Defaults live in `src/main/resources/pipeline.properties`.

Geocoding defaults to the free **US Census Geocoder** (no key). Geocodio is optional when a key is configured (`--geocoder=auto|census|geocodio|csv`).

For full structure, stages, data model, config, and open work, read **CONTEXT.md**. For why the scraper indexes unlisted pages, read **docs/BACKGROUND.md**. For CLI details, read **docs/CLI.md**. Deferred work lives in **tickets/**.

Do not rely on README.md alone for accuracy; use CONTEXT.md and the code.
